NNAAMMEE
     ccttllssttaatt — CAM Target Layer statistics utility

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ccttllssttaatt [--tt] [--cc _c_o_u_n_t] [--CC] [--dd] [--DD] [--jj] [--PP] [--ll _l_u_n] [--nn _n_u_m_d_e_v_s]
             [--pp _p_o_r_t] [--ww _w_a_i_t]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccttllssttaatt utility provides statistics information for the CAM Target
     Layer.  The first display (except for dump and JSON modes) shows average
     statistics since system startup.  Subsequent displays show average sta‐
     tistics during the measurement interval.

     The options are as follows:

     --tt          Total mode.  This displays separate columns with the total
                 read and write output, and a combined total column that also
                 includes non I/O operations.

     --cc _c_o_u_n_t    Display statistics this many times.

     --CC          Disable CPU statistics display.

     --dd          Display DMA operation time (latency) instead of overall I/O
                 time (latency).

     --DD          Text dump mode.  Dump statistics every 30 seconds in a text
                 format suitable for parsing.  No statistics are computed in
                 this mode, only raw numbers are displayed.

     --hh          Suppress display of the header.

     --jj          JSON dump mode.  Dump statistics every 30 seconds in Java‐
                 Script Object Notation (JSON) format.  No statistics are com‐
                 puted in this mode, only raw numbers are displayed.

     --PP          Prometheus dump mode.  Dump statistics in a format suitable
                 for ingestion into Prometheus.  When invoked with this op‐
                 tion, ccttllssttaatt dumps once, regardless of the --tt option.  This
                 option is especially useful when invoked by inetd(8).  See
                 the comments in _/_e_t_c_/_i_n_e_t_d_._c_o_n_f for an example configuration.

     --ll _l_u_n      Request statistics for the specified LUN.

     --nn _n_u_m_d_e_v_s  Display statistics for this many devices.

     --pp _p_o_r_t     Request statistics for the specified port.

     --ww _w_a_i_t     Wait this many seconds in between displays.  If this option
                 is not specified, ccttllssttaatt defaults to a 1 second interval.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
           ctlstat -t

     Display total statistics for the system with a one second interval.

           ctlstat -d -l 5 -C

     Display average DMA time for LUN 5 and omit CPU utilization.

           ctlstat -n 7 -w 10

     Display statistics for the first 7 LUNs, and display average statistics
     every 10 seconds.

